.\" "Generated by swift-argument-parser"
.Dd August 2, 2026
.Dt COCKER.DAEMON.RESIGN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm "cocker daemon resign"
.Nd "Re-sign cockerd with your Apple Development cert (post-brew-install)"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -identity Ar identity
.Op Fl -cockerd Ar cockerd
.Op Fl -entitlements Ar entitlements
.Op Fl -version
.Op Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Why this exists : `brew install cocker`'s post-install hook can't
read your login keychain  Homebrew sandboxes it away  so cockerd
ends up ad-hoc signed. That's fine for local boot, but the
TeamIdentifier is missing and the binary can't be moved between
machines. This command runs `security find-identity` outside the
sandbox, picks the first Apple Development (or Developer ID
Application) cert, and resigns the brew-installed cockerd with it.

Run it once after `brew install cocker` or `brew upgrade cocker`.

Override the cert by passing --identity "<full cert name>".
.Bl -tag -width 6n
.It Fl i , -identity Ar identity
Signing identity to use (defaults to the first Apple Development cert found).
.It Fl -cockerd Ar cockerd
Path to the cockerd binary to resign (defaults to /opt/homebrew/opt/cocker/bin/cockerd).
.It Fl -entitlements Ar entitlements
Path to the entitlements plist (defaults to /opt/homebrew/share/cocker/cockerd.entitlements).
.It Fl -version
Show the version.
.It Fl h , -help
Show help information.
.El
.Sh "EXIT STATUS"
.Ex -std